# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo on two separate counts, so they are
# pinned in the working tree on every platform rather than left to core.autocrlf:
#
#   1. PROMPT.md and md-mcp/docs/LOOP.md are byte-identical duplicates by design.
#      Without a rule here, git re-materialises one as CRLF without touching the
#      other and the contract breaks silently — the files still "look" the same.
#
#   2. tests/golden/, evals/corpus/holdout/ and evals/rubrics/ are hash-manifested
#      (LOOP §9.3), and manifests are verified before AND after every run. A CRLF
#      round-trip changes a file's SHA-256 without changing its content, which
#      presents as tampering and fails the iteration for a reason nobody can find.
#
# LF everywhere, including the checkout. Not just in the object store.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Hash-manifested and machine-compared files: never let a filter near these.
*.sha256    text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf

# Interchange formats are text and must round-trip byte-stably.
*.dxf       text eol=lf
*.obj       text eol=lf

# Marvelous Designer containers and assets — opaque, never diffed or filtered.
*.zprj      binary
*.zpac      binary
*.pac       binary
*.zmdr      binary
*.zfab      binary
*.avt       binary
*.arr       binary
*.pan       binary

# Ordinary binaries.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.7z        binary
*.dll       binary
*.pyd       binary
*.so        binary
